+## 3. Gap G-1 (the only FAIL root cause): CRLF `pm-state.md` phase is unreadable
+
+`StateManager.read()` (unchanged by this key) does:
+
+```ts
+for (const line of content.split("\n")) {
+    const m = line.match(/^- Phase:\s*(.+)$/);
+    if (m) state.phase = m[1].trim() as Phase;
+}
+```
+
+A CRLF file splits into lines ending in `\r`. In JavaScript, `.` does not match `\r` and `$`
+(without the `m` flag) does not match before a trailing `\r`, so the regex never matches:
+
+```
+[REGEX] line= "- Phase: DESIGN\r" match= false exec= null
+[SMOKE] crlf phase=undefined
+[SMOKE] lf phase="DESIGN"
+[SMOKE] real key phase=undefined
+```
+
+Repo-wide survey (`probe-survey.ts`, including the real key):
+
+```
+[VERIFY] survey: pm_state_files crlf=34 lf_only=6 missing=10 phase_parsed=6 phase_undefined=34
+[VERIFY] real-key: bytes=6311 crlf=67 lone_lf=0 StateManager.read().phase=undefined
+```
+
+Writer evidence:
+
+```
+python -X utf8 -c "p.write_text('- Phase: DESIGN\n', encoding='utf-8'); print(p.read_bytes())"
+bytes= b'- Phase: DESIGN\r\n'
+[RAW] advance_phase.py writes: ["396: pm_path.write_text(content, encoding=\"utf-8\")", "399: pm_path.write_text(", ...]
+```
+
+(The Python reader tolerates `\r` because Python's `.` matches `\r`, and `$` matches before a
+trailing `\n`; the bug is a JS/Python regex-behavior divergence on the same file bytes.)
+
+Pre-change behavior (why this is a regression introduced by this key):
+
+```
+git show ec93ac5a6:.../shared/phase-docs.ts
+export function phaseDocGaps(status: PhaseDocStatus): string[] {   // no tier
+    ... all 6 checks, unconditionally
+}
+```
+
+Before the change every dispatch from DESIGN onward was held to the full 6-item chain, so the
+phase-parse failure was harmless. After the change the 6-item chain is selected by
+`gateTierOf(phase)`, and on this machine `phase` is always `""` → spec tier → design side never
+checked.
+
+Impact:
+- VC-002, VC-003 (and AC-002/AC-003 semantics): DESIGN keys missing design docs/evidence are
+  dispatched instead of blocked — reproduced through all three real entrances.
+- D-110 site 1/2/3 all silently degrade to the spec layer on real bytes.
+
+Suggested fix (inside `agent-team-loop/**`, GC-2 allows it):
+`pm/state-manager.ts::read()` → `content.split(/\r?\n/)` (or normalize `\r\n` → `\n` first),
+plus a CRLF `pm-state.md` DESIGN-blocking fixture in `agent-team-loop-pm-state-sync.test.ts`
+so the test newline style matches the production writer. VC-002/VC-003 then turn PASS.
+
+Out of scope / not claimed here: this finding is about the *phase source*, not about the
+`gateTierOf`/`phaseDocGaps` pure functions, which are correct for a given phase string (VC-004,
+VC-005 PASS).
